  "skip_reason": "Layer-A canonical drive of `fv3_sinsg_flux_xi` requires ESS `discretize` to dispatch the cubed_sphere u_edge selector AND resolve the face-staggered metric bindings (`sin_pos`, `sin_neg`, `dx`) plus the scalar `dt` binding through the cubed_sphere grid accessor (`_precompute_sinsg_xi`). The cubed_sphere multi-axis selector / metric-binding extension is the same blocker that holds `lax_friedrichs_flux_cubed_sphere_xi` Layer-A at FAIL today; once that ESS extension lands, this fixture can be promoted to a hand-pinned canonical contract by mirroring the structure of `lax_friedrichs_flux_cubed_sphere_xi/fixtures/canonical/input.esm` (small cN cubed sphere, mixed-sign velocity covering both upwind branches and the `v=0` boundary case, dx and sin_pos/sin_neg drawn from the cubed_sphere grid accessor at u_edge stagger).",
  "reference_implementation": {
    "module": "EarthSciDiscretizations",
    "function": "compute_flux_with_sinsg_xi_arrayop",
    "path": "src/operators/wind_ops.jl",
    "comment": "Imperative reference for the metric-corrected ξ-direction flux. Follows Harris et al. (2021) §3.5, §6 (sub-grid sin(α) upwind selection) and Lin & Rood (1997) MWR. The closed-form upwind-blended flux ((v + |v|)·sin_pos + (v − |v|)·sin_neg)/2 · dx · dt is what the rule's `expression` block encodes; the per-cell `sin_pos`/`sin_neg` arrays are precomputed at u_edge by `_precompute_sinsg_xi` and exposed to the rule as scalar bindings via the cubed_sphere grid accessor."
  },
